{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Due}: Week 15 (Friday, December 11)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Points}: 5\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Submit to}: Blackboard\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Submission}: By Individual\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Instructions\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 There are two parts to this assignment: a {\b resume and cover letter review meeting}, and the {\b professional materials} themselves.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 A resume and cover letter review meeting\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Meet with Shannon from the Resume lecture slides. You may schedule your meeting via Orange SUccess, or you may use the email on the slides to make an appointment ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:srvanbev@syr.edu"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
srvanbev@syr.edu
}}}
).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li720 \fi0 {\b Important}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li720 \fi0 You must meet with Shannon or your advisor.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li1080 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab If you meet with {\b Shannon}, there is no need to submit any proof of meeting, as she will inform us which students met with her at the end of the year.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li1080 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab If you meet with a {\b different advisor}, have them email Prof.\u160 ?Reilly.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li1080 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab If you have already met with another advisor for resume and cover letter review this semester, you may email your UCA with proof.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li1080 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab If you have already met with Shannon this semester for resume and cover letter review, please email her to remind her.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Professional materials\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Your professional materials must include the following five items.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 1. A one-page professional resume\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 2. A one-page cover letter\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Tailored to the job or internship of your choice.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 3. A LinkedIn profile\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Your profile must include at least the following:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab A work-appropriate headshot for the profile\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab A completed \u8220"About\u8221" section\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Completed educational information\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab At least one professional experience. We strongly encourage using this course as a professional experience \u8211- the position name is \u8220"Research Consultant,\u8221" and the location is your client agency.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab A connection request sent to all UCAs and Professor Reilly\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 4. A one-page draft reference letter\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Written about yourself from a professor\u8217's perspective (Coplin, Professor Reilly, or someone else).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Include information a professor would reasonably know about you that describes your professional experiences and strengths.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab This is meant to help a professor write you a recommendation, so save this for future use. Should you ever request a recommendation from Coplin or Professor Reilly, they will ask for this letter.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 5. A draft Instagram post\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Written as a summary of your project for the Policy Studies Instagram.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Choose a photo for the post \u8211- either your client organization\u8217's logo, your photo from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "06-organizational-assessment.qmd"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Organizational Assessment
}}}
, or something similar.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Draft a caption. Include a short summary of your project and the most interesting finding, 1-2 sentences in length.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Tag yourself and your client.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab When you submit this, please indicate whether you consent to have your project featured on the Policy Studies Instagram page.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Files\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "files/instagram-post-template.docx"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Instagram Post Template
}}}
 (Word)\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 As always, your UCAs are available by email to answer any questions.\par}
